This file is a marker, not configuration. Its presence beside the SAAT
executable is what tells SAAT it was installed rather than unpacked, which
switches it from portable mode to installed mode:

    portable   watches/, config.toml and backups/ live beside the executable
    installed  the collection lives in %LOCALAPPDATA%\SAAT
               and settings in %APPDATA%\SAAT

Deleting this file makes SAAT portable again and it will stop finding a
collection stored in the locations above -- the data is not lost, but SAAT
will look for it beside the program instead.

Nothing reads the contents of this file. See SPEC.md section 2, rule 2.
